{"id":56916,"ord":97,"n_segments":158,"prev":56915,"next":56917,"doc":{"id":"68163","title":"68163_Tom Whaley oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Tom Whaley","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68163/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68163"},"chapter":"Will Vodery and the road shows","title":"The TOBA circuit and Wiley Avenue in Pittsburgh","category":"touring_travel","summary":"Hinton and Whaley explain the TOBA circuit, nicknamed Tough On Black Asses, and the show's stop on Wiley Avenue.","period":"c. 1924-25","year_from":1924,"year_to":1924,"words":161,"start":[124,5],"end":[125,12],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68163#s56916","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Pittsburgh","focus":1,"type":"city","in":"Pennsylvania"},{"name":"Wiley Avenue","focus":1,"type":"street","in":"Pittsburgh"}],"venues":[{"name":"Top of the Hill","focus":0,"city":"Pittsburgh"}],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Tom","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Eubie Blake","qid":"Q919632","n":1},{"name":"TOBA","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":13,"theme_name":"Medicine shows, minstrels, circuses and the black theater circuit","community":23,"community_name":"On the road with minstrel, carnival and tent shows","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":124,"b":5,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"And what's a TOBA?"},{"p":124,"b":6,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"Tough on Black Ass."},{"p":124,"b":7,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"That was our name for it, Tough On Black Ass. But the real name was what? It had to be something else."},{"p":124,"b":8,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"I don't know."},{"p":124,"b":9,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"There was a legitimate name for it."},{"p":124,"b":10,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"TOBA."},{"p":124,"b":11,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"This was a black show business circuit. And we called it Tough On Black Asses because it was so rough on us, on the road."},{"p":124,"b":12,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"That's right."},{"p":124,"b":13,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"But there was another name.*"},{"p":124,"b":14,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"And I remember in Pittsburgh, we was at"},{"p":124,"b":15,"s":"","x":"*Theatre Owners Booking Agency"},{"p":125,"b":0,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"this hotel, either the Top of the Hill or -- Wiley Avenue."},{"p":125,"b":1,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"Wiley Avenue, that's it. And --"},{"p":125,"b":2,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"What year is this, now, Tom?"},{"p":125,"b":3,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"Oh, this is way back."},{"p":125,"b":4,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Not too far back."},{"p":125,"b":5,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"No, it was around 24 or 25."},{"p":125,"b":6,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"I see. What show are you with now?"},{"p":125,"b":7,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"That's Stopping the Traffic."},{"p":125,"b":8,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Stopping the Traffic."},{"p":125,"b":9,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"Now, --"},{"p":125,"b":10,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"And you're the musical conductor?"},{"p":125,"b":11,"s":"MR. WHALEY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":125,"b":12,"s":"MR. HINTON","x":"Eubie Blake was the guy that did all -- conducted all them shows."}]}